# Streamlining Instructional Design: An Expedient Learning Analysis.

**Authors:** Toney, Michael R., White, Margaret C.

## Abstract
Discusses instructional design; examines various analyses which should be made as part of instructional development, including needs analysis, front-end analysis, job analysis, task analysis, training analysis, and learning analysis; and describes steps in a learning analysis that is less labor-intensive and time-consuming. A learning analysis checklist is included. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ464284

